LanternBoy: {
	DisplayName: The Lantern Boy
	Origin:
		'''
		On dark mountain paths, a pale white paper lantern often swings through the gloom, floating above a pair of bare, hovering children's feet that never touch the earth.
		Any nocturnal traveler who stares into the flame for more than three breaths finds their eyes sealed shut as if by hot wax, their soul dragged screaming into the paper skin.
		Three murdered surrogate souls are already sealed within; wherever that sickly light falls, lantern shadows move in tandem with the blade, striking in place of the wielder.
		'''
	Power: "「Guiding Light」Three pale ghost lanterns orbit your body, their lamplight casting shadows that echo your normal slashes off-beat for a combined sixty percent of their original power."
	DeathReason: "{0} was led into the fourth white paper lantern"
}

CrimsonBride: {
	DisplayName: The Crimson Bride
	Origin:
		'''
		Outside an isolated mountain manor stood a grand eight-bearer crimson palanquin with no living carriers in sight—only pale paper effigies painted with stiff, grinning faces.
		Whenever the curtain lifted a crack, sorrowful and shrill wedding horns echoed through the woods; whoever had their birth hour chosen was forced to wed in a silent, dead bridal hall.
		When a desperate blade-bearer calls upon this palanquin, it arrives bursting through the void across a trail of blood, receiving them into a funeral hall draped in mourning white and scarlet silk.
		At the moment of the nuptial cup, all fatal wounds and afflictions are dissolved by the hall, turning death back into life.
		'''
	Power: "「The Procession」Press the Self-Restart key and the grand crimson palanquin arrives riding sinister funeral music, welcoming the blade-bearer into a dead, blood-draped wedding hall; at the nuptial toast, all fatal wounds and afflictions are washed away and restarted."
	DeathReason: "{0} sat in the crimson palanquin and bowed to heaven and earth"
}

ScapeGhost: {
	DisplayName: The Scapegoat Wraith
	Origin:
		'''
		A crude straw doll wrapped in human hair and birth dates, its straw body scarred by thousands of fatal chest wounds and severed neck gashes.
		In life it took death's place for others countless times, its form battered and incomplete, long forgetting whose death was originally its own.
		The day it is bound to the register, your death omen is tied with twine around its straw neck.
		The instant doom falls, cold dead hands reach from the dark, violently forcing your mortal demise into the flesh of a nearby living creature.
		'''
	Power: "「Death's Stand-In」At the moment fatal catastrophe arrives, forcibly transfers your death onto a distant living creature, using their body to perish in your stead and escaping death."
	DeathReason: "{0} became the dead soul behind the straw surrogate"
}

HeadlessShade: {
	DisplayName: The Headless Shade
	Origin:
		'''
		Under the dim glow of midnight oil lamps, someone looked down and saw their own shadow squirming and crawling on the floor—and above its shoulders, there was nothing at all.
		This decapitated horror has long lurked in dead angles, ravenously craving to piece together a whole living body.
		It has stitched itself into the shadow beneath your feet; once it catches the scent of enemy life, it tears out from the floor, brutally ripping the prey into severed pieces.
		'''
	Power: "「Dismember」Lurking in the shadow beneath your feet, it surges from the ground upon sensing living prey, tearing their flesh into severed pieces with savage brutality."
	DeathReason: "{0}'s head was ripped clean off by the headless shade"
}

GhostHand: {
	DisplayName: The Charred Hand
	Origin:
		'''
		A carbonized limb dug from the ashes of cremated dead and charred infernos, its five claw-like fingers curled inward in a permanent, desperate grasp.
		None know what manner of sea of fire this corpse was trapped within, only that the suffocating malice of its strangling grip lingers unbroken across death.
		The moment it senses the warmth of living breath, the blackened claw erupts from the void behind, seizing the victim's throat and crushing bone to dust over and over.
		'''
	Power: "「Bone-Grip」A charred, withered ghost arm erupts from the void to seize prey by the throat, repeatedly crushing and suppressing their movement; when foes gather, more hands reach out to crush mighty enemies between their fingers."
	DeathReason: "{0} had every bone crushed to powder by the charred hand"
}

GhostRain: {
	DisplayName: The Ghost Rain
	Origin:
		'''
		An ominous gloom recorded in ancient scrolls that unleashes not sweet rain, but freezing black water reeking of silt and decomposing rot.
		Those who look up in terror find that beneath the clouds hang layer upon layer of pale, dead faces staring down with closed eyes.
		The black rain falls without physical pain, yet thousands of unseen corpse-leeches gnaw away marrow and soul; anyone soaked for three breaths melts like wax and is dragged into the mire.
		'''
	Power: "「Gloom-Shower」Holding the blade calls down an oppressive canopy of black clouds and pouring black rain; living things caught within have their flesh dissolved continuously, providing an aggressive targeting medium for other wraiths."
	DeathReason: "{0} was dissolved by black rain and dragged into the mud"
}

System: {
	ScapeGhostActivated: "{0} became the scapegoat"
	ScapeGhostUnknownTarget: a living creature
	ScapeGhostDeathBroadcast: "{0} became {1}'s scapegoat, {2}"
	ErosionCrawl: Something feels like cold corpse-worms crawling beneath your skin
	ErosionStain: Fingertips bloom with permanent, bruised corpse-spots
	ErosionMirror: The face reflected in the bronze mirror no longer looks like you
	RevivalStir: The vermilion birth date on the seal talisman twitched
	RevivalRise: That thing is staring intently at you through the yellow paper
	RevivalBrink: The seal talisman burns like branding iron, barely held in check
	RevivalHudBrink: The horror is on the verge of waking; one more act and it seizes you
}

Coven: {
	RainHandName: Reach in Rain
	RainHandNote: Prey soaked in black rain is no longer bounded by reach; the charred hand reaches straight down from the rain threads overhead. Up to five hands can manifest simultaneously in rain, and crushing damage doubles as the storm swells
	RainShadeName: Wet Blade
	RainShadeNote: While the wound left by the shade passing through remains unhealed, every tick of rain corrosion on that target deals double damage
	HandShadeName: Pinned to Sever
	HandShadeNote: The headless shade prioritizes pouncing on prey gripped by the charred hand; with target movement suppressed to zero, the executing slash never misses
	LanternHandName: Illumination
	LanternHandNote: Prey revealed by the ghost lanterns can be hunted by the charred hand even through stone and terrain; lantern blade-light deals 60% more damage to gripped targets
	BrideName: Bridal Hall
	BrideNote: Living creatures drawn into the bridal hall during the nuptial toast stop losing other wraith marks until the bridal hall disperses
	ScapeName: Averting Doom
	ScapeNote: When the straw surrogate dies in your stead, the revival state of all other wraiths on the same board is suppressed back by one tier
	CallName: Resonant Call
	CallNote: Wraiths on the same board wake one another: whenever one is commanded, the others gain a small amount of revival; even pairs without unique synergies resonate with dark hunger
	BurstName: Triple Mark Rupture
	BurstNote: Gathering three distinct wraith marks on a single target detonates multiple fatal curses at once for heavy burst damage, each participating wraith paying a revival cost
}
